From 1075856f975f7490542179587d5d9d0e5b892da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo Sachsenberg <sachsenberg@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:49:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [FIX] ProSE: deisotoping keeps fragment ions that have a
 small peak one isotope spacing below

ProSE deisotoped high-resolution MS2 spectra with Deisotoper's default start_intensity_check=2,
which lets the second peak of an envelope exceed the first. A small peak 1.00335 Da below a
fragment ion then became the envelope's monoisotopic peak and the ion itself was removed as its
isotope. Every TMT/TMTpro-labelled fragment has such a peak (reagent isotope impurity); on the
TMTpro files of the OpenMS#10364 benchmark this removed 18-21% of the fragment peaks that match
the identified peptide, and 5-6% on Orbitrap Astral and timsTOF spectra.

ProSE now requires isotope intensities to fall from the monoisotopic peak on
(start_intensity_check=1). A class test covers the TMTpro case and that regular 1+ and 2+
envelopes are still deisotoped. The TOPP references ProSE_1/2/4 change in scores and PSM
features only (identical hits); ProSE_4's calibrated fragment tolerance tightens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D1N3pC2AqJt57Q3v87bWxz
